label: Provenanced
description: >-
  blue-ribbon's `Field<T>` metadata, minus the value. Spread into any edge
  that carries a measured value, via `"...Provenanced":`.

  This is a WIN and I want to be fair about it. blue-ribbon wraps every card
  field as `Field<T> = { value, provenance, vintage }`, which at the storage
  boundary flattens into five columns per logical field (see
  packages/schema/src/duckdb-columns.ts -- 68 columns for 13 measurements).
  weir has no generics, so `Field<T>` cannot be declared once. But the field
  spread syntax gets me the four metadata fields without retyping them, and
  the `value` is declared per-edge with its real type. That is close enough to
  parametricity for this shape, and it is better than blue-ribbon's current
  situation where the five-column expansion is hand-written in
  duckdb-columns.ts AND hand-written again in store.ts's CREATE TABLE.

  FRICTION (#6) remains, and it is the one most relevant to weir's
  classification feature: `provenance` below is COMPUTED AT RUNTIME by
  combineProvenance -- a lattice meet over the sources that actually answered.
  weir's `classification:` is a STATIC declaration on a field. So blue-ribbon's
  trust lattice cannot be a weir classification, and weir's classification
  cannot be computed. They are the same algebra with different lifetimes, and
  weir currently supports only one lifetime. Two lattices, one mechanism, is
  the feature I actually want.
fields:
  provenance:
    type: utf8
    label: Provenance
    description: >-
      How much this value can be trusted, ranked verified > inferred >
      aggregator > listing claim. A value derived from several sources takes
      the weakest of them (combineProvenance in
      packages/schema/src/provenance.ts).
    nullable: false
    enumValues:
      - verified
      - inferred
      - aggregator
      - listing claim
  vintageAsOf:
    type: utf8
    label: Vintage As Of
    description: ISO date this value was true as of
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 10
      maxLength: 10
  vintageSourceType:
    type: utf8
    label: Vintage Source Type
    description: How often the underlying source changes
    nullable: false
    enumValues:
      - static
      - periodic
      - continuous
      - manual-confirmation
  vintageNote:
    # FRICTION: this is free text, and it is the one field on a card that can
    # carry anything at all. In blue-ribbon it holds methodology ("not yet
    # computed"), but nothing stops it holding an owner name someone pasted
    # while debugging. It should NOT inherit the classification of the value
    # it annotates -- which means a per-field label is right here and a
    # per-edge label would be wrong. Cuts in weir's favour.
    classification: freetext
    type: utf8
    label: Vintage Note
    description: Why this value is what it is, or why it is null
    nullable: true
    validations:
      maxLength: 500
